{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Conjectures.WeakSpectralCompleteness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Conjectures.WeakSpectralCompleteness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.WeakSpectralCompleteness.completeness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.WeakSpectralCompleteness.completeness","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/WeakSpectralCompleteness.lean#L89-L89","doc":"**Conjectural categorical completeness.**  Each projector is\nidempotent and distinct projectors are orthogonal — the\npairwise-orthogonal idempotent decomposition exhausting the EW\nWedderburn content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.WeakSpectralCompleteness.projector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.WeakSpectralCompleteness.projector","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/WeakSpectralCompleteness.lean#L84-L84","doc":"The six per-link block projectors `e_W^±, e_Z^±, e_H^±`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.WeakSpectralCompleteness.ring_EWAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.WeakSpectralCompleteness.ring_EWAlgebra","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/WeakSpectralCompleteness.lean#L82-L82","doc":"`EWAlgebra` is a (possibly non-commutative) ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.WeakSpectralCompleteness.EWAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.WeakSpectralCompleteness.EWAlgebra","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/WeakSpectralCompleteness.lean#L80-L80","doc":"The carrier algebra `End_R(V^{⊗6})` of the `n = 6` Hecke action. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.WeakSpectralCompleteness.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.WeakSpectralCompleteness.mk","kind":"ctor","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/WeakSpectralCompleteness.lean#L78-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.WeakSpectralCompleteness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.WeakSpectralCompleteness","kind":"class","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/WeakSpectralCompleteness.lean#L69-L91","doc":"**Conjecture class** (`conj:weak-spectral-completeness`).\n\nAn instance supplies the six per-link block projectors `e X ±` of the\nEW carriers `{T(2,4), T(2,6), T(2,8)}` inside `End_R(V^{⊗6})` and\nasserts that they form a **categorically complete pairwise-orthogonal\nidempotent decomposition** of the EW Wedderburn content.  The\n`completeness` field carries the genuine completeness claim (the\nprojectors are orthogonal idempotents exhausting the EW sector), not a\nbare `True`.  This is a **primary** conjecture. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.cellTrace_bar_self_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.cellTrace_bar_self_dual","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/WeakSpectralCompleteness.lean#L59-L67","doc":"**Bar T-duality at the trace level.**  The cell-content trace is\ninvariant under the bar involution `ι : q ↦ q⁻¹` — each summand\n`qⁿ + q⁻ⁿ` is manifestly bar-self-dual. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.cellTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.cellTrace","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/WeakSpectralCompleteness.lean#L49-L57","doc":"The bar-self-dual cell-content trace\n`tr_pure(σ₁⁴ σ₃⁶ σ₅⁸)`, as a Laurent expression in an invertible\n`q : R`:\n`4(q¹⁸+q⁻¹⁸) + 2(q¹⁰+q⁻¹⁰) + (q⁶+q⁻⁶) + 3(q²+q⁻²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.cellMultiplicities_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.cellMultiplicities_sum","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/WeakSpectralCompleteness.lean#L45-L47","doc":"The cell-content multiplicities sum to `20` (out of the\n`∑_{λ⊢6} f_λ = 76` seminormal-basis vectors). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.cellMultiplicities","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.cellMultiplicities","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/WeakSpectralCompleteness.lean#L41-L43","doc":"The eight pure-pattern cell-content multiplicities of the EW sector\n`(4, 2, 1, 3, 3, 1, 2, 4)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}